# Fighters Boxing Gym: Apache config for the Hostinger static deploy.
#
# Added 2026-09-19 with the blog rebuild. Two of the client's 10 original
# WordPress posts were retired because they could not carry evergreen
# content honestly:
#
#   billy-falco-named-interim-head-coach-...  a personnel announcement,
#       built almost entirely from quotes by a founder who has asked to
#       come off the blog, about a coach whose current status we have
#       never had confirmed. Sent to the Coaches page, which is the live
#       equivalent of what it was about.
#
#   jake-paul-vs-mike-tyson  dated celebrity commentary with no local
#       lead intent. The fight's whole story was a 58 year old boxing, so
#       it is sent to the post that owns the age question.
#
# 301 rather than delete: both URLs were published and may carry links.
# A 301 passes that equity to a live, relevant page. A 404 throws it away.

<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On

  # Retired posts. [R=301,L] with NC so a linked variant in the wrong case
  # still lands. The optional trailing slash covers both link forms.
  RewriteRule ^billy-falco-named-interim-head-coach-of-fighters-boxing-gym/?$ /coaches/ [R=301,L,NC]
  RewriteRule ^jake-paul-vs-mike-tyson/?$ /5-steps-to-start-boxing-at-any-age/ [R=301,L,NC]
</IfModule>

# No ErrorDocument line on purpose: this build has no 404 page yet, and
# pointing Apache at a file that does not exist is worse than its default.
# Worth adding one before launch now that two URLs are retired.
